{"id": "EUVD-2026-102564", "enisaUuid": "d20df3e3-9cf0-3189-b8fb-8a81d6b3029c", "description": "Nezha from 2.0.13 before 2.3.15 contains a resource exhaustion vulnerability that allows authenticated users to open unbounded concurrent connections to the /api/v1/ws/transfer WebSocket endpoint. Attackers can hold thousands of subscriptions created by ServerTransferClass.Subscribe without limits, exhausting file descriptors, memory, and goroutines and blocking agent gRPC reconnections.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T01:17:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T16:24:21", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/nezhahq/nezha/security/advisories/GHSA-ch6h-w872-77mx", "https://github.com/nezhahq/nezha/commit/36b742a7e9a81ed782363dd19efd77b7030fbd0f", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/nezha-2.0.13-before-2.3.15-denial-of-service-via-api-v1-ws-transfer-websocket"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111383", "GHSA-44hc-q89j-v46p"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.3, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "fec33f78-0e1e-37b1-9857-aeff9c0ea8ce", "product": {"name": "nezha", "vendor": {"name": "nezhahq"}}, "product_version": "2.0.13 <2.3.15"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e4729631-cc96-361a-9b84-6ea57ad9b4c7", "vendor": {"name": "nezhahq"}}], "isExploited": false}